  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-saving shelter and non-food item assistance for dignified living conditionsLife-saving shelter and non-food item assistance for dignified living conditions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is providing basic life-saving emergency shelter and non-food items (NFI) support to people affected and displaced by the floods primarily in southern Punjab, Pakistan where dire needs persist. The current situation in Punjab reflects a combination of riverine and flash flooding, where water levels continue to rise in rivers&#x2014;both from upstream discharges (Indian side) and heavy local rainfall&#x2014;resulting in inundation of settlements. IOM&#x2019;s support ensures the most vulnerable affected and displaced families in Punjab have access to basic shelter and NFI to save lives, ensure dignity in displacement and avoid potentially rapidly deteriorating protection and health conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
